[profiles.guide]
notes = '''Star Wars: Empire at War + Gyro: tilting the controller moves the cursor too, as a fine pointer next to the right stick {rs}. Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller.
The right stick {rs} moves the cursor: {rt} or {south} selects (left click, hold to drag a box), and {lt} moves or attacks (right click). The left stick {ls} scrolls the camera, {updown} zooms and {r3} resets the camera.
{north} is attack and {west} stop: press attack, then pick the target with {rt}. {left} and {right} step to the previous and next unit; {l3} selects every unit.
Hold {lb} for the control groups and aim the right stick {rs} at one: release to select it. Hold {lb} and {rb} together to put the selection in a group instead (Ctrl + number).
Hold {rb} for the unit orders (guard, move, waypoint, retreat, reinforce, the units of one type, the superweapon), aimed with the right stick {rs}. A unit's own abilities are on its buttons at the bottom of the screen: click them with {rt}.
{select} lists the tactical overview, the mission holocron, planet information, the player list, chat and the cinematic camera.
{start} (Esc) is the game menu. Double-tap {start} to quick save and hold it to quick load. {east} cancels and closes.
The game has no controller support of its own, so the controller works through these keys. They're the defaults as remembered by a community FAQ, not checked on an install: if one does nothing, look in Options, Controls. Hold {guide} and press {west} for the on-screen keyboard (chat, save names).'''

